        "round_idx": 0
      },
      {
        "node_id": "c4",
        "uuid": "60529d39-26cb-4ae8-8774-b3d4797fbb86",
        "type": "claim",
        "text": "The posterior shadowing observed in the mass is a feature that can be associated with both benign and malignant lesions. While it is more commonly seen in cystic lesions, it can also be present in solid lesions.",
        "label": "MALIGNANT",
        "label_int": 1,
        "expert_id": "expert_b",
        "round_idx": 0
      },
      {
        "node_id": "c5",
        "uuid": "e0b0fa7e-b90b-463d-805f-8efcfb6a4426",
        "type": "claim",
        "text": "The non-parallel orientation of the mass, as seen in the image, is not necessarily indicative of a benign lesion. In fact, a non-parallel orientation can be a sign of malignancy, particularly when combined with other features such as irregular margins or heterogeneous echo pattern.",
        "label": "MALIGNANT",
        "label_int": 1,
        "expert_id": "expert_b",
        "round_idx": 0
      },
      {
        "node_id": "c6",
        "uuid": "35719400-1902-4078-bcee-5a4d4191afe5",
        "type": "claim",
        "text": "The irregular margin observed in the mass is a key feature that suggests malignancy. Irregular margins are typically associated with malignant lesions and can be more difficult to define compared to the circumscribed margins seen in benign lesions.",
